WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.170 --> 00:00:08.641
-(CROWD CHEERING)
-ANNOUNCER:<i> It's showtime!</i>

00:00:09.409 --> 00:00:11.277
RODNEY BARNES:
The year is 1979,

00:00:11.344 --> 00:00:14.080
and the Los Angeles Lakers
are, if you can believe it,

00:00:14.247 --> 00:00:15.447
a down-and-out team.

00:00:15.514 --> 00:00:17.250
JERRY BUSS:<i> Welcome
 to sunny Los Angeles.</i>

00:00:17.350 --> 00:00:19.785
<i> Great for tans,
 shit for fans.</i>

00:00:20.052 --> 00:00:21.687
RODNEY: But the new owner
has a vision.

00:00:21.787 --> 00:00:24.290
JERRY:<i> If there's two things
that make me believe in God,</i>

00:00:24.390 --> 00:00:26.158
<i> it's sex and basketball.</i>

00:00:26.359 --> 00:00:28.227
RODNEY: Welcome to
the world of<i> Winning Time,</i>

00:00:28.427 --> 00:00:30.596
the new HBO series
about the rise

00:00:30.696 --> 00:00:31.831
of the Lakers dynasty.

00:00:32.231 --> 00:00:35.301
ANNOUNCER 2:<i> First pick
 of the 1979 NBA draft,</i>

00:00:35.434 --> 00:00:37.770
<i> the Los Angeles Lakers
 select</i>

00:00:37.937 --> 00:00:40.640
<i> Earvin "Magic" Johnson.</i>

00:00:41.707 --> 00:00:42.541
RODNEY: I'm Rodney Barnes,

00:00:42.708 --> 00:00:44.677
an executive producer
and writer on the show,

00:00:44.743 --> 00:00:47.980
and the host of
the official<i> Winning Time</i>
companion podcast

00:00:48.080 --> 00:00:50.383
from HBO,
Hyperobject Industries,

00:00:50.450 --> 00:00:52.318
and Pineapple Street
Studios.

00:00:54.754 --> 00:00:57.189
Over the next ten weeks,
I'll be breaking down

00:00:57.256 --> 00:00:58.825
each episode
of<i> Winning Time,</i>

00:00:59.158 --> 00:01:00.693
taking you
behind the scenes,

00:01:00.793 --> 00:01:02.495
and talking shop
and basketball

00:01:02.595 --> 00:01:05.331
with the show's creators,
stars and collaborators.

00:01:05.565 --> 00:01:08.701
Everyone from
executive producer
and director, Adam McKay...

00:01:08.935 --> 00:01:10.537
ADAM MCKAY: When you get
that fast-break,

00:01:10.637 --> 00:01:12.806
freewheeling,
creative style going,

00:01:12.906 --> 00:01:15.741
it's much harder
to game plan against.

00:01:15.841 --> 00:01:17.610
So these teams
started winning

00:01:17.777 --> 00:01:20.046
and they were winning
with style and flair.

00:01:20.146 --> 00:01:22.014
And right in the middle
of that

00:01:22.281 --> 00:01:24.183
were the Showtime Lakers.

00:01:24.283 --> 00:01:26.118
RODNEY: ...to showrunner
Max Borenstein...

00:01:26.319 --> 00:01:28.088
MAX BORENSTEIN: I hope that
one of the things

00:01:28.154 --> 00:01:31.457
people come away with
is not just an appreciation

00:01:31.557 --> 00:01:33.092
for the people
that they know,

00:01:33.159 --> 00:01:35.828
the Magics, the Kareems,
the Pat Rileys,

00:01:35.995 --> 00:01:38.331
but knowing and respecting
and having

00:01:38.431 --> 00:01:40.132
a new appreciation
for the characters

00:01:40.199 --> 00:01:41.734
and the people
that they've never heard of.

00:01:41.834 --> 00:01:45.037
RODNEY:
...to the breakout star who
plays Magic Johnson himself,

00:01:45.137 --> 00:01:46.372
Quincy Isaiah.

00:01:46.472 --> 00:01:47.640
QUINCY ISAIAH:
I feel like sometimes,

00:01:47.740 --> 00:01:51.010
I have to remind myself
like, "Yo, you doing this.

00:01:51.077 --> 00:01:53.079
You here because
you deserve to be here."

00:01:53.646 --> 00:01:55.914
If I feel like an imposter,
all right, well,

00:01:55.981 --> 00:01:58.150
let's work until I'm not.

00:01:58.550 --> 00:02:01.153
RODNEY: And along the way,
we'll learn how the Lakers

00:02:01.253 --> 00:02:03.756
came to be the center
of sports and celebrity

00:02:03.823 --> 00:02:04.891
in 1980s LA.

00:02:05.158 --> 00:02:07.593
JERRY:
<i> If you're a human being
 with two eyes and heart,</i>

00:02:07.693 --> 00:02:10.963
<i> this game, this industry
 makes you feel good.</i>

00:02:11.063 --> 00:02:12.798
JESSIE BUSS:
<i>What industry? Sweat socks?</i>

00:02:12.865 --> 00:02:14.266
JERRY:<i> No. Show business!</i>

00:02:14.566 --> 00:02:16.202
MAGIC JOHNSON:
<i>It's going to be exciting.</i>

00:02:16.368 --> 00:02:18.705
RODNEY:
<i> Winning Time: The Rise
 of the Lakers' Dynasty</i>

00:02:18.771 --> 00:02:21.774
premieres Sunday, March 6th
on HBO Max.

00:02:21.941 --> 00:02:25.144
Episode one of this podcast
drops right after that.

00:02:25.310 --> 00:02:26.512
Be sure to subscribe to

00:02:26.613 --> 00:02:29.415
<i>Winning Time: The Official
 Companion Podcast.</i>

00:02:29.649 --> 00:02:31.651
New episodes drop
every Sunday.

00:02:31.851 --> 00:02:34.888
Get them on HBO Max
or wherever you listen.

